    "summary": "High‑octane Fillmore East night with soaring guitar and front‑center Pigpen organ",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering Hard To Handle, monster Alligator jam and a luminous Morning Dew. Jerry’s lead work is on fire while Ron \"Pigpen\" McKernan’s organ sits prominently in the mix. Soundboard recordings capture the set’s tight transitions and high energy throughout.",
    "review": "April 29 1971 at the Fillmore East finds the Dead locked in a fiery groove that still feels fresh decades later. The first set rolls through classic covers and originals—Truckin', Bertha, Bird Song and Dark Hollow—setting up a second‑set launchpad of pure momentum. Hard To Handle erupts with Jerry’s soaring lead tone, while the Alligator/Drums/Alligator sequence builds into an expansive jam that segues seamlessly into Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad and Cold Rain And Snow. The night’s centerpiece is the China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider pair, where Pigpen’s organ blazes through the mix, adding a rare front‑and‑center texture for 1971. Morning Dew closes the set with an emotional high, and the encore—Uncle John’s Band into In The Midnight Hour—leaves the audience buzzing.\n\nAcross all available soundboard sources the performance is consistently praised: Jerry’s guitar struts, Phil “drops bombs” on bass during the Alligator excursions, Bob Weir provides solid rhythmic chops, and Bill Kreutzmann’s tight drumming underpins every transition. Ron \"Pigpen\" McKernan’s organ shines brighter than usual, giving the night a distinctive tonal color. The Miller multitrack capture (gd1971-04-29.sbd.multitracks.miller.114350.flac16) delivers crystal‑clear separation and brings out those organ swells, making it the definitive listening choice for this legendary Fillmore East outing.",
